// QUIC's variable-length integers, RFC 9000 §16:
// https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000#section-16
//
// Two bits of the first octet say how many octets the integer occupies, so a
// small number costs one octet and a large one costs eight. Nearly every field
// in QUIC is written this way, which is why this is its own package and why it
// has no dependencies.
